From a39ba90ace77db86809b899af3cfe623d27b3c17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:42:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 652/689] aros: place Chromium's own codec worker threads off
 the media core

Chromium replaces the libvpx and libaom thread implementations with
CodecWorkerImpl, so their decode workers are base::Threads rather than
direct pthread_create calls, and the pthread_create wrapper never saw
them. They inherited the media thread's CPU, leaving VP9 row-MT decode on
one core.

CodecWorkerImpl now starts its thread under ScopedArosCodecThreadPlacement,
and PlatformThread places threads started in that scope round-robin on
CPUs 1..N-1 when --aros-pin-codec-threads is given. 1080p high-bitrate VP9
on 4 CPUs over 90 s: 23.9 fps / 165 dropped unplaced, 29.8 fps / 6 dropped
with the codec workers placed, 28.3 fps / 137 dropped with every thread
pinned (--aros-pin-workers).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHhVavHvnUWcvCukPGJBkG
